pt.md:18:- Each arm tip launches a \"turtle\" heading 90° right of its outward direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:19:- Movement priority: turn right > go straight > turn left (left only if not on border).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:20:- Normal step = 2 cells; step right after a turn = 1 cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:21:- Each new cell must have a 1-cell orthogonal gap from all existing walls except the predecessor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:22:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:23:Key insight: The right-turn preference plus alternating 2/1 step lengths creates self-avoiding spirals that tile the grid with uniform spacing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:24:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:25:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:26:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:27:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b5ca7ac4\" lines=\"7-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:28:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:29:Move bordered 5×5 squares to their designated grid edges by border color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:30:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:31:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:32:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:33:- Azure (8) and red (2) bordered 5×5 squares with colored interiors, scattered across the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:34:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:35:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:36:- Azure squares → left edge (col 0); red squares → right edge (col W−5).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:37:- Each square keeps its original row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:38:- Process azure left-to-right, red right-to-left (nearest-to-edge first).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:39:- If a square's rows overlap an already-placed edge square, place it one square-width inward instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:40:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:41:Key insight: Near-edge-first ordering plus row-overlap determines which square sits at the edge vs. the second column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:42:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:43:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:44:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:45:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"db695cfb\" lines=\"8-19\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:46:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:47:Connect same-color diagonal pixel pairs, then emit perpendicular rays from differently-colored pixels on those diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:48:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:49:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:50:- bg = most common color. Line color (e.g. blue) has pixel pairs aligned on shared diagonals. Trigger color (e.g. magenta) pixels sit along those diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:51:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:52:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:53:- Draw diagonal lines connecting each pair of same-color aligned pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:54:- Where the diagonal crosses a trigger pixel, emit perpendicular diagonal rays (in the trigger's color) extending to the grid boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:55:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:56:Key insight: Trigger pixels act as beam-splitters — the perpendicular rays rotate 90° from the connecting diagonal's orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:57:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:58:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:59:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:60:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"16de56c4\" lines=\"9-34\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:61:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:62:Fill periodic progressions that shoot from a unique grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:63:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:64:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:65:- bg = most common color.  Sparse non-bg dots of several colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:66:- All repeating colors originate from the same grid edge (top, bottom,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:67:  left, or right — the one with the most non-bg dots).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:68:- Each repeating color has exactly 2 dots per shooting-direction line;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:69:  their gap defines the step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:70:- Every non-bg dot lies on a shooting-direction line that contains a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:71:  repeating color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:72:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:73:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:74:- Determine the unique shooting edge; left/right → rows, top/bottom → columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:75:- For each shooting-direction line, the repeating color has exactly 2 dots;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:76:  step = gap between them, offset = first position mod step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:77:- A different-colored dot aligned to the same beat (pos % step == offset) is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:78:  a companion: it absorbs the ray and becomes the fill color, limiting the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:79:  fill range to the span between repeating and companion dots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:80:- An unaligned dot is a bystander and left untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:81:- Without a companion the repeating color fills the entire line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:82:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:83:Key insight: the shooting edge is identified by counting boundary dots;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:84:the gap between the two marker dots is the period; a companion sharing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:85:modular class acts as a wall that stops the ray and dictates the paint color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:86:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:87:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:88:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:89:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"62593bfd\" lines=\"32-46\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:90:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:91:Sort objects to top or bottom edge by whether their shape (up to rotation/flip) is shared.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:92:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:93:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:94:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:95:- Several multicolor connected components (8-connected) scattered across the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:96:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:97:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:98:- Compute each object's canonical shape (binary mask, invariant to rotation and flip).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:99:- Objects whose shape appears in two or more components → translate to TOP edge (row 0).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:100:- Objects whose shape is unique → translate to BOTTOM edge (row H−h).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:101:- Horizontal position (left column) is preserved; only vertical translation changes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:102:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:103:Key insight: The sorting criterion is shape frequency (rotation-invariant), not area — duplicated shapes go up, unique shapes go down.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:104:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:105:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:106:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:107:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"fc7cae8d\" lines=\"9-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:108:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:109:Align a central rectangle to two colored frame-edge controls via rotation/reflection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:110:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:111:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:112:- bg grid with two solid-colored border edges (distinct non-bg colors).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:113:- A central filled rectangle with 1px colored guide edges on two sides, colors matching the frame controls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:114:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:115:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:116:- Rotate/mirror the object so its guide edges face the same sides as the matching frame controls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:117:- Crop off the 1px guide edges from aligned sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:118:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:119:Key insight: Guide-edge colors encode target frame sides; the correct dihedral transform matches both simultaneously.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:120:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:121:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:122:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:123:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"45a5af55\" lines=\"5-18\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:124:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:125:Build nested square frames from a stack of horizontal color stripes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:126:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:127:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:128:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:129:- Each stripe has uniform color and variable height (1-4 rows).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:130:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:131:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:132:- Read stripes bottom to top.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:133:- Bottom stripe becomes the center solid square with side length = stripe height.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:134:- Each subsequent stripe wraps the current shape with a square frame of thickness = stripe height, in that stripe's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:135:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:136:Key insight: Stripe height doubles as both frame thickness and (for the innermost) center-square side length; output dimensions are fully determined by the stripe heights.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:137:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:138:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:139:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:140:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"3a25b0d8\" lines=\"9-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:141:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:142:Fill holes in a target object with colors from a source object's subsprites, then tight-crop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:143:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:144:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:145:- bg = background. Two similar 8-connected objects share an outline color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:146:- Source has colored subsprites in cavities; target has empty cavities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:147:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:148:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:149:- Find the two 8-connected objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:150:- Target = object with more hole area. Align subsprites to holes (rotation/flip if needed).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:151:- Fill each hole with its matched subsprite color; tight-crop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:152:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:153:Key insight: Hole centers in the target are matched to source subsprite centers under the best rotation/flip transform.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:154:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:155:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:156:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:157:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"6ffbe589\" lines=\"83-98\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:158:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:159:Crop a board cluster and rotate its color layers based on outside cue sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:160:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:161:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:162:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:163:- A main multi-color board cluster (largest foreground region).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:164:- Small monochrome cue sprites outside the board for the colors that rotate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:165:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:166:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:167:- Tight-crop around the board cluster.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:168:- For each color layer inside the crop, find its same-color cue outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:169:- Rotate that layer clockwise by (cue pixel count mod 4) × 90°.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:170:- No outside cue → no rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:171:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:172:Key insight: Cue sprite size mod 4 encodes rotation amount for its matching color layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:173:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:174:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:175:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:176:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"c4d067a0\" lines=\"9-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:177:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:178:Complete a grid of colored blocks to match a minimap legend in the top-left corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:179:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:180:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:181:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:182:- Top-left corner: a small sprite of single colored pixels forming a minimap pattern on a regular lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:183:- Main area: uniformly colored square blocks (NxN) arranged on a regular grid; some positions are empty (bg).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:184:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:185:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:186:- The legend pixels define a color pattern; each pixel's lattice position maps to a block position in the main grid via a fixed scale factor and offset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:187:- Existing colored blocks confirm the scale/offset alignment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:188:- For every legend pixel whose corresponding grid position is empty, place a new block of that color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:189:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:190:Key insight: The top-left pixel pattern is a scaled-down minimap of the block layout; the mapping is inferred from blocks already present.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:191:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:192:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:193:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:194:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"f560132c\" lines=\"259-273\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:195:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:196:Assemble scattered jigsaw pieces into a rectangle, recoloring each by a legend sprite's color map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:197:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:198:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:199:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:200:- Several monochrome non-bg sprites (the \"pieces\"), scattered across the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:201:- One sprite is the legend: it contains a multi-color k×k patch (typically 2×2) encoding output colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:202:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:203:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:204:- Tile all pieces (rotations/reflections allowed) into a tight rectangle with no gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:205:- The legend's k×k color patch defines a spatial color map over the rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:206:- Each piece is recolored to the legend-map color corresponding to its position in the assembled rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:207:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:208:Key insight: The legend piece doubles as both a jigsaw piece and a color key — its internal k×k palette assigns colors by spatial quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:209:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:210:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:211:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:212:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"78332cb0\" lines=\"10-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:213:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:214:Reorder 5×5 blocks into a connected strip by matching edge foreground pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:215:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:216:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:217:- bg = background; sep = divider color (full row/column lines).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:218:- Several 5×5 sprite blocks in a grid, separated by sep lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:219:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:220:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:221:- Two blocks \"connect\" when their facing edges share foreground pixels at the same offset (e.g., A's right edge ∩ B's left edge).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:222:- Chain all blocks in the orientation (horizontal or vertical) that admits a complete sequence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:223:- Output is a 1×N strip of blocks in chain order, separated by sep lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:224:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:225:Key insight: Edge-contact overlap determines both block ordering and output orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:226:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:227:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:228:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:229:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"7491f3cf\" lines=\"9-24\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:230:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:231:Composite two pattern tiles into a fourth panel using flood-fill from an indicator pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:232:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:233:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:234:- Four 5×5 panels in one row, border-separated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:235:- Panel 0: cue pixels = wall boundary (8-connected, edge-to-edge, through center)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:236:           + one 8-isolated indicator pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:237:- Panels 1–2: source patterns. Panel 3: blank (to fill).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:238:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:239:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:240:- Flood-fill (4-conn) from indicator, blocked by wall → inside region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:241:- Inside → non-bg from panel 1; outside → non-bg from panel 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:242:- Wall → panel 1 if non-bg; panel 2 fallback when wall is 4-connected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:243:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:244:Key insight: The cue panel's isolated indicator and wall partition the tile into inside/outside masks that select between the two source panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:245:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:246:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:247:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:248:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"195c6913\" lines=\"37-52\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:249:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:250:Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:251:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:252:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:253:- Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:254:- Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:255:- A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:256:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:257:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:258:- Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:259:- On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:260:- Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:261:- If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:262:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:263:Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:264:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:265:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:266:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:267:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b9e38dc0\" lines=\"7-18\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:268:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:269:Fill the region enclosed by a wall sprite and radiate color outward through its opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:270:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:271:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:272:- bg = most common color. Wall = most frequent non-bg color, forming a partial enclosure (e.g. U-shape).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:273:- A fill-color pixel sits inside the enclosed area. Other non-bg pixels may act as obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:274:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:275:- Flood-fill the enclosed area with the fill color, radiating outward through the wall's open end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:276:- Obstacles cast \"shadows\" along the radiate direction, blocking fill behind them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:277:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:278:Key insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:279:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:280:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:281:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:282:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"65b59efc\" lines=\"9-24\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:283:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:284:Decode a stamp map: read templates, markers, and palette from a tiled grid, then render stamps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:285:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:286:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:287:- Grid divided into K tile columns (each N wide) separated by 1-col dashed separators.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:288:- Top band (rows 0..N-1): K template masks, one per tile column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:289:- Middle band (rows N+1..2N): marker pixels whose color picks a template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:290:- Bottom band (rows 2N+2..): K palette swatches giving the output color per template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:291:- Separator rows at rows N and 2N+1 (dashed pattern of sep color).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:292:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:293:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:294:- Each marker's local position (lr, lc) within its tile column determines which N×N output block to stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:295:- The marker's color identifies which template to use; the palette recolors the template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:296:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:297:Key insight: Marker color encodes template index; local position within tile column encodes stamp block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:298:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:299:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:300:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:301:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8698868d\" lines=\"9-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:302:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:303:Match sprites to frames by connected-hole count, then nest each sprite inside its frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:304:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:305:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:306:- bg = azure (8). Large hollow squares (frames) arranged in a grid; smaller filled squares (sprites) placed elsewhere.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:307:- Each frame and sprite has a distinct color. Sprites may contain holes (non-sprite-color pixels).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:308:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:309:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:310:- Frames form a regular grid; some may be bg-colored (invisible).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:311:- Count connected hole regions inside each frame's interior and each sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:312:- Pair each frame with the sprite sharing the same hole count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:313:- Place the matched sprite inside the frame border; recolor sprite holes to the frame's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:314:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:315:Key insight: The matching key is the number of connected hole components, not hole area or color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:316:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:317:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:318:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:319:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"db0c5428\" lines=\"32-51\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:320:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:321:Expand a 3x3 block motif into a 5x5 block motif around its missing center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:322:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:323:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:324:- Teal background surrounds one 9x9 foreground motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:325:- The motif is a 3x3 array of 3x3 blocks; the middle block is empty teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:326:- Colored pixels immediately around the empty middle block encode the border\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:327:  of the missing center block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:328:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:329:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:330:- Keep the original 9x9 motif in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:331:- Copy each of the eight surrounding 3x3 blocks to the opposite outer slot\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:332:  of the implied 5x5 block grid, without rotating it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:333:- Fill the center block from the eight pixels around the hole; its center is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:334:  the motif's majority foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:335:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:336:Key insight: The visible 9x9 motif is the middle of a larger periodic\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:337:block-level pattern, and the empty center is reconstructed from its immediate\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:338:inner boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:339:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:340:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:341:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:342:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"d8e07eb2\" lines=\"29-47\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:343:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:344:Look up query glyphs in a reference table and mark whether they form a line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:345:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:346:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:347:- Teal background with two full-width pink separator rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:348:- Above the first separator is a query row of 5x5 glyph cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:349:- Between separators is a reference table of the same 5x5 cells; a glyph is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:350:  identified by both its color and its 3x3 shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:351:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:352:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:353:- Green-fill the background inside every table cell whose glyph exactly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:354:  appears in the query row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:355:- If the matched table cells form one complete row or one complete column,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:356:  also green-fill the query band and the bottom verdict band.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:357:- Otherwise leave the query band unchanged and fill the bottom verdict band red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:358:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:359:Key insight: The bottom color is not a count; it is the yes/no answer to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:360:whether the queried glyphs align as a full row or column in the table.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:361:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:362:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:363:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:364:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2d0172a1\" lines=\"209-224\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:365:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:366:Convert a rough nested line drawing into a clean canonical frame-and-dot diagram.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:367:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:368:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:369:- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:370:- Foreground 4-connected objects are rough closed frames or small filled blobs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:371:- Frames may contain other frames/blobs; blobs outside a frame remain outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:372:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:373:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:374:- Detect the containment tree of foreground objects using holes of each frame object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:375:- Replace every blob with one foreground pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:376:- Replace every frame with a rectangular border padded two cells around its direct children.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:377:- Place siblings by their original row/column overlap and order, with one empty cell between canonical objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:378:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:379:Key insight: The exact wobbly geometry is irrelevant; only enclosure plus relative sibling positions define the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:380:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:381:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:382:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:383:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:384:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:385:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:386:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:387:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:388:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:389:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:390:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:391:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:392:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:393:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:394:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:395:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:396:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:397:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:398:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:399:请一次性生成 5 个 `<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:400:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:401:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:402:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:403:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:404:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:405:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:406:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:407:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:408:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:409:6. 5 个新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:410:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:411:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:412:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:413:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:414:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:415:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:416:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:417:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:418:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:419:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:420:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:421:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:422:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:423:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:424:3. 可实现性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:425:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:426:4. ARC 合规性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:427:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。没有使用上述注意事项第二条禁止使用的复杂计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/prompt.md:428:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:1:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:2:- `description`：根据色带宽度确定折叠轴，将网格沿轴对折后用覆盖色合并两层像素。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:3:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:4:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:5:  - bg = black。网格为矩形，包含若干彩色像素图案。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:6:  - 网格的某一条边（上、下、左或右）紧贴着一条宽度为 1-3 像素的纯色色带（色带颜色与图案颜色均不同）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:7:  - 色带仅出现在一条边上，其余三条边无色带。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:9:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:10:  - 第一层推理——确定折叠轴与折叠方向：色带所在边即为折叠的\"铰链边\"。例如色带在左边，则沿左边缘垂直轴向右对折；色带在上边，则沿上边缘水平轴向下对折。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:11:  - 第二层推理——确定折叠偏移量：色带的宽度（像素行数或列数）决定折叠后两层之间的偏移量。宽度为 1 则完全对齐折叠；宽度为 2 则折叠后上层相对下层偏移 1 个像素（沿折叠方向）；宽度为 3 则偏移 2 个像素。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:12:  - 折叠后输出网格的尺寸 = 折叠方向上原尺寸的一半（向上取整）加上偏移量，另一方向尺寸不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:13:  - 两层像素合并规则：若某位置两层都有非背景色像素，则输出色带的颜色；若只有一层有非背景色像素，保留该颜色；若两层都是背景色，保持背景色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:14:  - 色带本身不出现在输出中。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:15:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:16:- `Key insight`：色带的位置编码折叠轴，色带的宽度编码折叠偏移——两者必须同时正确识别才能产生唯一输出；重叠处统一变为色带颜色是合并信号而非简单覆盖。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:17:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:18:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:19:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:20:- `description`：在网格中找到被围栏圈定的区域，按区域内种子像素的颜色和数量生成向内收缩的同心轮廓。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:21:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:22:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:23:  - bg = black。网格中有若干用 grey 像素绘制的封闭围栏（围栏为 1 像素宽的闭合矩形环，各围栏互不重叠、互不嵌套）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:24:  - 每个围栏内部散布着 1-4 个相同颜色的\"种子\"像素（不同围栏内种子颜色可不同）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:25:  - 围栏外部均为背景色，不含任何非背景像素。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:26:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:27:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:28:  - 第一层推理——确定收缩层数：每个围栏内部种子像素的数量 N 决定该围栏内需要绘制 N 圈向内收缩的同心矩形轮廓。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:29:  - 第二层推理——确定轮廓颜色与绘制方式：所有同心轮廓均使用该围栏内种子的颜色绘制。第 1 圈轮廓紧贴围栏内壁（即围栏内侧第 1 行/列），第 2 圈在第 1 圈内侧再缩 1 像素，以此类推。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:30:  - 围栏本身（grey 像素）保持不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:31:  - 种子像素被同心轮廓覆盖或位于轮廓上时直接融合（颜色相同故视觉无变化）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:32:  - 若围栏内空间不足以容纳 N 圈轮廓，则只绘制能容纳的层数（向内缩到无法形成完整环为止）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:33:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:34:- `Key insight`：种子数量不是装饰而是指令——它编码了需要绘制多少层同心环；解题者必须同时将\"计数\"与\"几何收缩\"关联起来，才能得到正确输出。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:35:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:36:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:37:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:38:- `description`：将散落的形状碎片按颜色匹配拼入对应颜色框架的内部空腔，拼入前需根据框架缺口朝向旋转碎片。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:39:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:40:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/5/des.md:41:  - bg = black。网格中有若干彩色矩形框架（仅